328 - Must Jesus Bear the Cross Alone
 / 
Key: C
Time: 4/4
Tempo: Moderato
Number: 328
Topic: Gospel - 

Verse 1:
[G]Must Jesus bear the cross [Am/C]alone, [C]and all [G/B]the [D7/C]world [G/B]go free?
[G]No, there's a cross for [Am/C]everyone, [C]and there's [G]a cross [Dm]for [G]me.

Verse 2:
[G]The consecrated [C]cross [D7/C]I'll [G]bear
[G]till He shall [C]set me [G/B]free;
[G]and then go [Am/C]home [C]my crown [G]to [Dm]wear,
[G]for there's [Am/C]a [C]crown [G/B]for me.

Verse 3:
[G]Upon the crystal [C]pavement, [G]down
[G]at Jesus' [C]pierced [D7/C]feet,
[G]with joy I'll [Am/C]cast [C]my golden [Dm]crown,
[G]and His dear [C]name repeat.
